<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Crimean Socialist Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1919 CE · capital Simferopol</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bolshevik republic in the Crimea in spring 1919, headed by Lenin's brother Dmitry Ulyanov and ended by the White advance.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In April 1919 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> broke into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/crimean-regional-government">Crimean Regional Government</a>, and the Bolsheviks proclaimed the Crimean Socialist Soviet Republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-ulyanov">Dmitry Ulyanov</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin">Lenin</a>'s younger brother, became deputy chairman and effective head of its council of people's commissars.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was intended partly to reassure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-tatars">Crimean Tatars</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> had its own government. It nationalised land, banks and industry and set up a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> of the Crimea. Allied warships and White troops still held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch">Kerch</a> peninsula, so its control was never complete.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In June 1919 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armed-forces-of-south-russia">Armed Forces of South Russia</a> landed and advanced into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, and the Soviet government withdrew. The Crimea remained in White hands until November 1920, when the Bolsheviks returned for good.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/crimean-socialist-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Crimean Socialist Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Simferopol</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dmitry Ulyanov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Crimean SSR (1919)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=crimean-socialist-soviet-republic" aria-label="Crimean Socialist Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5492 590 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Crimean Socialist Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5812 846L5812 846M5812 846L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5812 846h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5812 846h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5812 846h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Simferopol. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=crimean-socialist-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

